/-!
# The ruling data of the T-twisted Crauder–Katz link

This is the T-twisted analogue of `Submission/Work/MotK/RuleData.lean` (which handles the split
data with the shift-invariant quadric `q = kleinQ = Σ_k kleinP k`).  For the *T-twist* the
relevant quadric is the image of `p₀`, i.e. `kleinTwQ = kleinTwP0`, and the quadratic map is the
twisted Pfaffian map `kleinTwP`; the inverse map is `kleinTwR`.

The design's node `K5` gives the ruling of the two exceptional divisors of the twisted
quadro-cubic link by the explicit lines

  `ℓ_c = ℙ(span(A(c), B(c)))`,  `A(c) = dP_c(u₁)`,  `B(c) = dP_c(u₂)`,

where `P = kleinTwP a b h`, `u_j = b_q(c, e_j)·e₀ − b_q(c, e₀)·e_j` is the tangent vector of the
twisted quadric `q = kleinTwQ` at `c`, and `dP_c(u) = kleinTwP (c+u) − kleinTwP c − kleinTwP u`
is the polarisation of the quadratic map in the direction `u`.  The claim is

* **(ruling)** `kleinTwR (λ·A(c) + μ·B(c)) ∝ c`  (`kleinTwR` is projectively constant on `ℓ_c`),

for `c ∈ C`; equivalently `ℓ_c` is contained in the fibre of `kleinTwR` over `c`, and hence — by
the twisted I2 (`KleinTwI2inv`: `kleinTwP (kleinTwR z) = kleinTwSDualV z • z`) — in the ruling
divisor `{s' = 0}`: `kleinTwP (kleinTwR w) ∝ kleinTwP c = 0` for `w ∈ ℓ_c` gives
`kleinTwSDualV w • w = 0`, so `kleinTwSDualV w = 0` for `w ≠ 0`.  This is the ruling of the
*target-side* exceptional divisor of the twisted Crauder–Katz link.

**Warning (a *false* companion statement, tested and refuted).**  The quadratic map itself is
*not* projectively constant on `ℓ_c`: `kleinTwP (λ·A(c) + μ·B(c)) ∝ c` is FALSE.  Counterexample
(two reviewers, independently): `a = b = h = 1`, `λ = 1`, `μ = 2`, `c = (0,-7,-7,7,7)` (which
satisfies all five twisted quadrics) gives `w = A + 2B = (0,49,-49,49,-49)` and
`kleinTwP w = (0,-4802,-4802,-4802,-4802)`, whose `(1,3)`-minor with `c` is `-67228 ≠ 0`.  The
fibre of `kleinTwP` over `[c']` is the *linear* space `{x : M(x)·c' = 0}` (the twisted form of
`Work.MotK.CensusFibre.kleinFibre_eq_ker`), not a line of the ruling `ℓ_c`; the two are related by
the `F`-side of the link, with `c'` ranging over the residual curve `C'` and not over `C`.

Note `A(c)₀ = B(c)₀ = 0`: the ruling lines lie in the hyperplane `{w₀ = 0}`, the chart of the
target side of the link.

The identity is the *input* of the census of the certificate `Work.MotK.LinkCertT`; it is proved in
the sibling file `KleinTwRuleMem.lean` (**(ruling)**).

**Certificate existence, checked independently of any Gröbner implementation.**  For
`(a,b,h) = (2,3,5)` and `(λ,μ) = (1,2)`, the difference `D_ij = R_i(ℓ_c)·c_j − R_j(ℓ_c)·c_i` is
homogeneous of degree `7` in `c`, and the linear system "`D_ij = ∑_k g_k·kleinTwP_k` with `g_k`
homogeneous of degree `5`" has `1260` unknowns against `330` equations of rank `295`; the
augmented matrix has the *same* rank `295`, so the system is solvable and `D_ij` lies in the
ideal generated by the five twisted quadrics.  (Same rank as in the split case of
`CensusFibre.ruling_mem`, as it must be: the twisted data is the Kummer twist of the split data.)

**A transcription trap.**  The five twisted quadrics `kleinTwP a b h` are polynomials in the
*coordinate* vector; when the Gröbner basis (or the linear certificate) is built for an identity
in the variables `c`, the quadrics must be substituted into the variables `c`.  Reducing with a
basis consisting of `kleinTwP a b h` in *unsubstituted* variables reports a nonzero normal form
and makes the identity look false; it is not.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false

namespace Work.MotK

variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R]

/-- The tangent vector `u_k = b_q(c,e_k)·e₀ − b_q(c,e₀)·e_k` of the T-twisted quadric
`q = kleinTwQ = kleinTwP0` at `c` (design `K5`).  Since `b_q` is the polar form of `q`, one has
`b_q(c, u_k) = 0`, i.e. `u_k` lies in the tangent space `T_c {q = 0}`. -/
def kleinTwTan (a b h : R) (c : Fin 5 → R) (k : Fin 5) : Fin 5 → R :=
  fun i => kleinTwBilin a b h c (kleinE k) * kleinE 0 i
    - kleinTwBilin a b h c (kleinE 0) * kleinE k i

/-- The polarisation of the quadratic twisted Pfaffian map `P = kleinTwP a b h` at `c` in the
direction `u`: `dP_c(u) = kleinTwP (c+u) − kleinTwP c − kleinTwP u`, componentwise. -/
def kleinTwPolarP (a b h : R) (c u : Fin 5 → R) : Fin 5 → R :=
  fun i => kleinTwP a b h (c + u) i - kleinTwP a b h c i - kleinTwP a b h u i

/-- The first ruling vector `A(c) = dP_c(u₁)`. -/
def kleinTwRuleA (a b h : R) (c : Fin 5 → R) : Fin 5 → R :=
  kleinTwPolarP a b h c (kleinTwTan a b h c 1)

/-- The second ruling vector `B(c) = dP_c(u₂)`. -/
def kleinTwRuleB (a b h : R) (c : Fin 5 → R) : Fin 5 → R :=
  kleinTwPolarP a b h c (kleinTwTan a b h c 2)

/-- The point `λ·A(c) + μ·B(c)` of the ruling line `ℓ_c`. -/
def kleinTwRulePt (a b h : R) (c : Fin 5 → R) (l m : R) : Fin 5 → R :=
  fun i => l * kleinTwRuleA a b h c i + m * kleinTwRuleB a b h c i

end Work.MotK
